  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation Farmers for Green Growth: Promoting Sustainable Agricultural Value Chains in Asia-Pacific</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The action aims to empower farmers, farmers&#xbf; organisations, and cooperatives, as well as to promote agroecological value chains and food systems. The action will enhance linkages between farmer&#xbf;s organisations and cooperatives with local and international agribusinesses (traders, processing companies, food industry), financial institutions and research organisations. Strong- and consolidated farmers&#xbf; organisations are key to develop inclusive and sustainable agricultural value chains in Asia and Pacific, as well as to scaling up and out agroecological food systems. The action will have two components: (1)The first one will support Asian and Pacific farmer&#xbf;s organisations at continental, regional, and national levels. This component will specifically support technical and economic services provided by farmers&#xbf; organisations, with a strong focus on agroecological transition, as well as enhance linkages between farmers&#xbf; organisations and cooperatives with local agri-SMEs and international large firms. (2)The second component aims to contribute to a sustainable agri-food system transition based on agroecological principles in Asia and the Pacific through to the operationalization of a Regional Multi-Actor Research Network on Agroecology and the improvement of tool(s) on agroecological performance measurement and use for policies.</narrative>
  </description>
